<tool id="gappa_assign" name="GAPPA assign" version="@TOOL_VERSION@+galaxy@VERSION_SUFFIX@" profile="@PROFILE@">
    <description>assign taxonomy from phylogenetic placements</description>
    <macros>
        <import>macros.xml</import>
    </macros>
    <xrefs>
        <xref type="bio.tools">gappa</xref>
    </xrefs>
    <expand macro="requirements"/>
    <version_command>gappa --version</version_command>
    <command detect_errors="exit_code"><![CDATA[
gappa examine assign --jplace-path '$jplace' --taxon-file '$taxon_file' --threads "\${GALAXY_SLOTS:-1}"
    $per_query_results $krona $sativa
    ]]></command>
    <inputs>
        <expand macro="placements"/>
        <param argument="--taxon-file" type="data" format="tabular" label="Reference taxon assignments" help="Two tab-separated columns: reference-tree leaf name and semicolon-separated taxonomic lineage."/>
        <param argument="--per-query-results" type="boolean" truevalue="--per-query-results" falsevalue="" checked="false" label="Output per-query assignments"/>
        <param argument="--krona" type="boolean" truevalue="--krona" falsevalue="" checked="false" label="Output Krona profile"/>
        <param argument="--sativa" type="boolean" truevalue="--sativa" falsevalue="" checked="false" label="Output SATIVA assignments"/>
    </inputs>
    <outputs>
        <data name="profile" format="tabular" from_work_dir="profile.tsv" label="${tool.name} on ${on_string}: taxonomy profile">
            <actions>
                <action name="column_names" type="metadata" default="LWR,fract,aLWR,afract,taxopath"/>
                <action name="column_types" type="metadata" default="float,float,float,float,str"/>
            </actions>
        </data>
        <data name="labelled_tree" format="newick" from_work_dir="labelled_tree.newick" label="${tool.name} on ${on_string}: labelled reference tree"/>
        <data name="per_query" format="tabular" from_work_dir="per_query.tsv" label="${tool.name} on ${on_string}: per-query assignments">
            <filter>per_query_results</filter>
            <actions>
                <action name="column_names" type="metadata" default="name,LWR,fract,aLWR,afract,taxopath"/>
                <action name="column_types" type="metadata" default="str,float,float,float,float,str"/>
            </actions>
        </data>
        <data name="krona_profile" format="tabular" from_work_dir="krona.profile" label="${tool.name} on ${on_string}: Krona profile">
            <filter>krona</filter>
        </data>
        <data name="sativa_results" format="tabular" from_work_dir="sativa.tsv" label="${tool.name} on ${on_string}: SATIVA assignments">
            <filter>sativa</filter>
            <actions>
                <action name="column_names" type="metadata" default="name,taxopath,confidence"/>
                <action name="column_types" type="metadata" default="str,str,str"/>
            </actions>
        </data>
    </outputs>
    <tests>
        <test expect_num_outputs="2">
            <param name="jplace" value="placements.json"/>
            <param name="taxon_file" value="taxonomy.tsv"/>
            <output name="profile" file="profile.tsv">
                <metadata name="column_names" value="LWR,fract,aLWR,afract,taxopath"/>
                <metadata name="column_types" value="float,float,float,float,str"/>
            </output>
            <output name="labelled_tree" file="labelled_tree.newick"/>
        </test>
        <test expect_num_outputs="5">
            <param name="jplace" value="placements.json"/>
            <param name="taxon_file" value="taxonomy.tsv"/>
            <param name="per_query_results" value="true"/>
            <param name="krona" value="true"/>
            <param name="sativa" value="true"/>
            <output name="profile" file="profile.tsv">
                <metadata name="column_names" value="LWR,fract,aLWR,afract,taxopath"/>
                <metadata name="column_types" value="float,float,float,float,str"/>
            </output>
            <output name="per_query" file="per_query.tsv">
                <metadata name="column_names" value="name,LWR,fract,aLWR,afract,taxopath"/>
            </output>
            <output name="krona_profile" file="krona.profile"/>
            <output name="sativa_results" file="sativa.tsv">
                <metadata name="column_names" value="name,taxopath,confidence"/>
            </output>
        </test>
    </tests>
    <help format="markdown"><![CDATA[
Assign taxonomic lineages from **existing phylogenetic placements**, retaining their likelihood weights.

### Inputs

- A jplace JSON dataset from EPA-ng or pplacer. Its reference tree defines the placement edges.
- A headerless, two-column tabular dataset mapping reference-tree leaf identifiers to semicolon-separated taxonomic lineages. Leaf identifiers must match the jplace reference tree.

For example, `reference_1` may map to `Bacteria;Cyanobacteria;Synechococcus`.

### Outputs and interpretation

The taxonomy profile summarizes placement mass for each lineage. `LWR` and `fract` describe direct weight and its fraction; `aLWR` and `afract` include descendant taxa. `taxopath` is the semicolon-separated lineage. The labelled reference tree records the assigned lineages on the reference topology.

Enable **per-query assignments** to inspect the same quantities for individual query names. Enable **SATIVA assignments** for one lineage and a semicolon-separated list of confidences per query. Enable **Krona profile** for a weight followed by separate lineage columns; its width depends on the taxonomy depth.

A high placement weight supports a position relative to this reference. It does not establish that the reference taxonomy is correct or complete. Compare competing assignments before interpreting ambiguous sequences. This tool does not align sequences or perform placement searches.
    ]]></help>
    <expand macro="citations"/>
</tool>
